					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1372582&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606702949" alt="Jacob Conwell" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1372582)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jacob-conwell" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1372582); return false;" >Jacob Conwell</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606702918 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Nov 2020 02:21</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13859201/looking-for-greenlight-an-scp-music-stand-not-a-jojo-referen">[LOOKING FOR GREENLIGHT] An SCP Music Stand (Not a Jojo Reference)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831708">
									

<p>Directed here by PM:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Enough instruments playing the song on it manifest entities that appear to reenact actions based on the song being played, though if it’s played near a stage the effects are focused onto the stage, showing the actual events in question reenacted.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How close to the stage does this need to be? Additionally, how do they know there are events being portrayed by the music? If I just typed a random mix of letters onto a piece of paper and placed it on the anomaly, and had the music directed to a stage, what kind of events would this be?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Depending on the song the events range from benign to XK Class to a local area if uncontained.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, see, the thing with XK class events is if they happen there isn't really bouncing back from that, so you might need to tone down the power here a smidge, or at least have it presumed.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Watching too many of these turn certain people into cult-like groupie's that can make destructible but anomalous duplicates through unknown means.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So&#8230; a compulsion effect? Doesn't that seem a bit cliche?</p>
<p>With respect to the central narrative, you seem to focus more on Ixmer, almost to the point where I have to wonder what's the point of having the music stand item associated with this, since it seems like you have a lot more you care to write about this entity.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An SCP file left on it by accident reveals a major connection with one to The Factory, showing the entity using assets to buy out the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>That comes across as a very shoe-horned way of getting the Factory involved in this skip. While you obviously can include what ever GoI you want, this reads like you are including the Factory for the sake of including the Factory.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>All in all, you have a lot of moving parts to this skip, but none of them really congeal together. I'd argue focusing on Ixmer would be the strongest move, as the rest of the pieces you include here seem more like after thought in comparison, and I only imagine would bog the piece as a whole down.</p>

							</div>

								
					
