<p>This is already brilliant.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A cokehead grows ashamed of himself one day and decided to smash a few of his video games. He gets the bright idea to snort the fragments and discovers that doing so gives him a significantly weaker version of the main character's powers/skills/abilities/etc.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This alone was hilarious to me, overall however your concept feels like it's leaning towards the comedic side as opposed to anything else. If you want you could go a whole lot of different directions, this could be a tragedy, a comedy, an emotional piece, or anything really. Your concept has amazing versatility!</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Turns out, he kept a secret weapon all him all along; it's a little glass vial filled with fragments of a copy of Persona 5. He snorts it, magically dons a really beat up, low quality edgy black trenchcoat that smells like it hasn't been washed since Persona 1's release date.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I can't even begin to imagine how much the foundation would struggle to describe this seriously.</p>
<p>It's hard for me to really give much advice as you've got a solid concept and narrative. I'd definitely suggest looking into the copyright side of things, just to make sure you can make the references you want. If you do decide to work on this, I think it'd be a great main site article.</p>

							</div>

