			<div class="content" id="post-content-4831640">
									

<p>This is pretty good feedback. I don't really have a good answer for this atm, except that I imagined this one as more of a tragedy than a mystery.</p>
<p>One thing though, this SCP is a guy who isn't able to figure it out. At the very least, he hadn't even considered any outside entity could perceive things between lifetimes, and since he is imperfect each life he lives is usually fairly different. There's no real consequences for him either, as even if he were to get the chair he just starts over. This means he is fully willing to do some sideways stuff just to see what happens to him.</p>
<p>Some Thoughts I have to answer this below. I don't think these are complete, and welcome feedback.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Upon being discovered through a combinations of bad choices(no consequences really, if you think about it) and bad luck, he basically just kinda walks right into containment without realizing it. Think like a criminal who is so careless they kinda just wander into the cage, though to be entirely fair there hasn't yet been a cage that could ever hold him in any kind of permanent way.</p>
<p>An Idea I had been playing with was that he could claim to never have lived to old age. Everyone in his immediate family routinely live to their 90's, but he claims he's never gotten past 43. Not for lack of trying either, nor does he believe he has died of natural causes. He is <em>always</em> killed by un-natural means, whether that be by drowning, hanging, electrocution, being shot, or the world ending in some wild and sometimes anomalous fashion. He hasn't ever heard of the foundation before, at least to his knowledge, but he's definitely come into contact with anomalous ends in past lives.</p>
<p>I want his longest life to have been as a poacher, who got crushed to death in a stampede <em>he</em> caused. As he is currently in his mid-30's, this obviously alarms them, and inconveniences him as he's been trying to grow old for as long as he can remember and now he seems dead-ended with the foundation. I could have him become thaumial, interviewing him periodically to see if he experiences any end of the world scenarios, allowing them to &quot;brute force&quot; incoming end of the world scenarios, though any such attempt would likely challenge or overwhelm the Exclusion site's storage capacity.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

