<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> I have no clue</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>A cokehead grows ashamed of himself one day and decided to smash a few of his video games. He gets the bright idea to snort the fragments and discovers that doing so gives him a signifcantly weaker version of the main character's powers/skills/abilities/etc.</li>
<li>Example: snorting Super Mario Bros lets him jump 18 feet in the air. The catch? He'll break his ankles when he lands.</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+What&nbsp;the&nbsp;heck&nbsp;did&nbsp;I&nbsp;just&nbsp;write...?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-Uhh....</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>After spending much of his life disappointing his family, friends and divorced spouse, he goes on a downward spiral and then discovers his anomalous ability.</li>
<li>At first, he tries to do good.</li>
<li>He tries to help an old lady cross the road by snorting Super Mario Bros, picking her up and jumping across the street. It doesn't end well.</li>
<li>Then he snorts Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild and gets the Master Sword. He attempts to stop a bank robbery. However, he has no formal sword training and ends up dropping it, firing the Master Sword energy beam and accidentally killing someone's dog. The robbers then kick his ass and leave.</li>
<li>He finally decides to go down the road of villainy instead.</li>
<li>He snorts a copy of Megaman and tries to rob a bank. He ends up burning his hand off because it turns out human flesh isn't made to rapid fire concentrated plasma shots.</li>
<li>The Foundation finally notices him and tries to contain him.</li>
<li>He snorts a copy of Grand Theft Auto and tries to steal a car.</li>
<li>Well, he steals a car, alright.</li>
<li>He can't drive and ends up crashing into a fire hydrant.</li>
<li>The Foundation catch up to him.</li>
<li>Turns out, he kept a secret weapon all him all along; it's a little glass vial filled with fragments of a copy of Persona 5. He snorts it, magically dons a really beat up, low quality edgy black trenchcoat that smells like it hasn't been washed since Persona 1's release date.</li>
<li>He tries to summon Arsene and all he gets is a floating top hat that fires a tiny glob of darkness. All it does it make the Foundation Agent sneeze.</li>
<li>He gets contained.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Um. Well. He snorts things.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<p>Possible copyright issues? I forgot to give a movie and book as an example. Oh well.</p>
</div>
